          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In full generality, an
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-representation
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebraic
            structure on some object in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category
            up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent"} coherent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %em representation up to homotopy
            or maybe
            %em sh-representations
            \.
          %p
            We motivate the general notion of
            = succeed "-representation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            aspects of the ordinary notion of representation, and then leading over to the analogous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theoretic
            notions.
          %h3#representations_as_functors Representations as functors
          %p
            Recall that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G = (G \stackrel{\to}{\to})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            the category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            are equivalently
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                  %mi Vect
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{B}G \to k Vect
                  \\,.
          %p
            Such a functor takes the single object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            to some vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and takes every morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (* \stackrel{g}{\to} * )
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            labeled by an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
            to a linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g) : V \to V
            such that composition and the identity is respected. We have an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Rep
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Func(\mathbf{B}G, k Vect) \simeq Rep_k(G)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect
            could be replaced by other categories and they need not be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            or otherwise linear for the above to make sense. For instance if we take instead the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            itself, then a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{B}G \to Set
          %p
            is what is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            one is interested in representations in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{B}G \to Top
                  \\,.
          %p
            (However, rarely is it sufficient to regard these just as functors to the 1-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            here as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            and regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : \mathbf{B}G \to Top
            as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#IdeaInfRepresentations"} ∞-Representations
          %p
            Moreover, we may replace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            by a more general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            any groupoid, a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi k
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : K \to k Vect
          %p
            is called a linear representation of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in Vect
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_x
            for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \stackrel{g}{\to} y)
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is assigns a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g) : V_x \to V_y
          %p
            For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = \Pi_1(X)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \Pi(X) \to vect
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} flat
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
          %p
            And we do not even need to assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            here is a groupoid. For instance if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(D)
            its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+category"} path category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Vect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F(D) \to Vect
          %p
            is called a
            = succeed "-representation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p One could in principle therefore speak of a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F(D) \to Set
          %p
            as a “quiver permutation representation”, but there does not seem to be much use of this terminology in practice. The examples do show, however, that there is considerable overlap between the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            and of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            \.
          %h3#structured_representations_as_morphisms_in_2toposes Structured representations as morphisms in 2-toposes
          %p
            Still a bit more generally, we can speak of representations that preserve extra structure, such as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-sheaves"} (2,1)-sheaves
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
          %p
            We may also promote the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            to this
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi VectBund
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
            the groupoid of smooth
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi VectBund
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{B}G \to VectBund
          %p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(C)
            is a
            %em smooth representation
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g) : V \to V
            depend smoothly on the point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
          %p
            We can recover the underlying ordinary representation by applying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma : Sh_{(2,1)}(C) \to Grpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} \in C
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
          %p This yields the underlying bare representation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi Vect
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma(\rho) : \mathbf{B}G \to Vect
                  \\,.
          %p
            Conversely, one finds that extending such a bare representation from the point to all test spaces in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            amounts to equipping it with smooth structure.
          %p
            As before, this is not restricted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
            objects: we may replace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            here with any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}_1(X)
            is smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+groupoid"} path groupoid
            a representation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi VectBund
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{P}_1(X) \to VectBund
          %p
            as a morphism in the 2-topos is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{P}_1(X) \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            for more details and references.
          %p
            By just changing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            here, we can implement other geometric structures. For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+group"} algebraic group
            we may think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
            over something like the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fppf-site"} fppf-site
            structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi CAlg
                    %mi k
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = CAlg_k^{op}
            on formal duals of commutative
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            In this case there is a well-known good generalization of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi VectBund
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VectBund
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-topos"} (2,1)-topos
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi A
                  %mi Mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC : Spec A \mapsto A Mod
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right we have the groupoid of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            and hence a representation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{B}G \to QC
          %p
            of an algebraic group is a representation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on a vector space.
          %p
            But also here we may allow the represented structure to have more than one object. For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            regarded as an object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(C)
            a representation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in the context of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC
            is a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi QC
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : X \to QC
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaf
            of modules on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            one representation space, only that in a scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            there are no morphisms that would act on these.
          %p
            But more generally for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : K \to QC
          %p
            assigns to each point of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_0
            a representation space, such that these glue together to a quasicoherent sheaf of modules, and to each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            a morphism between the corresponding representation spaces, as before.
          %p
            Analogous constructions are available for more general sites, effectively we can take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+Lawvere+theory"} algebras over a Lawvere theory
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            that contains the theory of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            we are back to the smooth case discussed before.
          %p
            Also notice that if we take the site to be the point,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = *
          %h3#IdeaInfRepresentations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-Representations
          %p We have found above the term “representation” is, to a large extent, congruent with the term “morphism in a (2,1)-topos with codomain a stack of modules”.
          %p
            This way of thinking of representations has an immediate generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            and in particular to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %p
            To start with the simple discussion over the point again, a model for a notion of a category of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(k)
            that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
          %p
            If again
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            (equivalently: a “strong homotopy-functor” or “homotopy coherent functor”, see there for details)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : \mathbf{B}G \to Ch_\bullet(k)
          %p assigns
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                to the single obect of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                a chain complex
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\bullet
            %li
              %p
                to a group element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in G
                a chain map
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ρ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mo •
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g) : V_\bullet \to V_\bullet
            %li
              %p
                to a pair of group elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g, g'
                a chain homotopy
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g,g') : \rho(g')\circ\rho(g) \Rightarrow \rho(g' g)
                ;
            %li
              %p
                to a triple of group elements a homotopy of homotopies between composites of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ″
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g,g'), \rho(g,g'')
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ″
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g',g'')
                and so on
              %p
                (see the diagrams at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
                for more details in low degree).
          %p
            In other words, this is much like representation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as before on an ordinary vector space, only that now the action property of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
            holds only
            %em
              up to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent"} coherent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            \. Therefore people also speak of
            %em representations up to homotopy
            (
            %a{:href => "#AbadCrainic"}> AbadCrainic
            ) as well as
            %em strong homotopy representations
            and many other variants.
          %p
            As before, there is in principle no reason to restrict oneself to representations of groupoids here. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            or even
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            (recall the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            representations) and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+modules+over+an+algebra+over+an+operad"} model structure on modules over an algebra over an operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : K \to Mod
          %p
            an
            = succeed "-representation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            If we wish to consider
            = succeed "-generalizations" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            itself, then an
            = succeed "-permutation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \to \infty Grpd
          %p
            is known as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaf"} (∞,1)-presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of an ordinary group or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} equivariant homotopy
            theory. Notice that by the
            = succeed "-theorem" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\infty Grpd \simeq Top
          %p
            so that the above is equivalently an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \to Top
          %p
            hence literally a
            %em representation up to homotopy
            in the classical sense of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %p
            As before, all this may be lifted from the point into large classes of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "-representation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            There are then analogs of the above relation between representations of path groupoids and connections on bundles. For more on this see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport"} higher parallel transport
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            there is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+in+a+locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{P}(X)
            of any object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}(X)
            define general abstract
            %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity,1)-topos#FlatDifferentialCohomology"} flat differential cohomology
            and
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+system"} local system
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            (see there for some more properties and examples).
          %p
            For instance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-geometry"} dg-geometry
            is the study of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            of formal duals of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi A
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC : Spec A \mapsto A Mod
          %p
            on this site, where now however
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            (or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            if we do a more comprehensive discussion) of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            ove the dg-algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            then a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : X \to QC
          %p
            is a equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+%E2%88%9E-stack"} quasicoherent ∞-stack
            of modules on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-representation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            If one replaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            here by its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+space"} de Rham stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
            then dg-algebraic
            = succeed "-representations" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                  %mo →
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho : X_{dR} \to QC
          %p
            are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-module"} D-module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            A discussion of these higher categorical structure in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#Ben-ZviNadler"}> Ben-ZviNadler
            ).
          %h3#representations_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            \-Representations
          %p
            If the codomain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            that is just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-category"} (n,1)-category
            (all
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphisms"} k-morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \gt n
            are effectively identities) then an
            = succeed "-representation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-representation
            %em representations up to homotopy
            where from degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            on all homotopies are actually identities:
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            representations up to homotopy.
          %p
            As always in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            are more restrictive but typically admit a more tractable detailed analysis and construction.
          %p
            2-representations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groups"} 2-groups
            and
            = succeed "s" do
